[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:26. Wanted: A Large Biscuit Tin]
[00:00.700] Passage 26 | 文章26
[00:02.510] Wanted: A large biscuit tin. | 征求：一个大饼干罐。
[00:06.830] No one can avoid being influenced by advertisements. | 没有人能避免受广告的影响。
[00:11.445] Much as we may pride ourselves on our good taste, | 尽管我们可能为自己的好品味而自豪，
[00:14.670] we are no longer free to choose the things we want. | 我们已不能自由选择我们想要的东西了。
[00:17.840] For advertising exerts a subtle influence on us. | 因为广告对我们施加着一种微妙的影响。
[00:21.365] In their efforts to persuade us to buy this or that product, | 在他们努力说服我们购买这种或那种产品时，
[00:25.015] advertisers have made a close study of human nature | 广告商对人性进行了深入研究，
[00:28.455] and have classified all our little weaknesses. | 并将我们所有的弱点都分了类。
[00:31.965] Advertisers discovered years ago that all of us love to get something for nothing. | 广告商多年前就发现，我们所有人都喜欢不劳而获。
[00:37.960] An advertisement which begins with the magic word "free" | 一则以“免费”这个神奇词语开头的广告
[00:42.095] can rarely go wrong. | 很少会出错。
[00:44.185] These days, advertisers not only offer free samples, | 如今，广告商不仅提供免费样品，
[00:48.895] but free cars, free houses, | 还有免费汽车、免费房屋，
[00:51.770] and free trips around the world as well. | 以及免费环球旅行。
[00:54.840] They devise hundreds of competitions which will enable us to win huge sums of money. | 他们设计了数百种竞赛，使我们能够赢得巨额奖金。
[01:00.630] Radio and television have made it possible for advertisers to capture the attention of millions of people in this way. | 广播和电视使广告商能够以这种方式吸引数百万人的注意力。
[01:07.560] During a radio program, | 在一个广播节目中，
[01:10.180] a company of biscuit manufacturers once asked listeners to bake biscuits | 一家饼干制造商曾要求听众烘焙饼干，
[01:15.100] and to send them to their factory. | 然后寄到他们的工厂。
[01:17.315] They offered to pay $2 a pound for the biggest biscuit baked by a listener. | 他们承诺以每磅2美元的价格购买听众烘焙的最大饼干。
[01:23.765] The response to this competition was tremendous. | 这次竞赛的反响非常热烈。
[01:27.095] Before long, biscuits of all shapes and sizes began arriving at the factory. | 不久，各种形状和大小的饼干开始陆续运到工厂。
[01:31.960] One lady brought in a biscuit on a wheelbarrow. | 有一位女士用独轮车运来一块饼干。
[01:34.955] It weighed nearly 500 pounds. | 它重达近500磅。
[01:37.855] A little later, a man came along with a biscuit which occupied the whole boot of his car. | 不久之后，一位男士带来一块饼干，它占据了他汽车的整个后备箱。
[01:43.225] All the biscuits that were sent were carefully weighed. | 所有寄来的饼干都经过仔细称重。
[01:46.895] The largest was 713 pounds. | 最大的一块重713磅。
[01:50.835] It seemed certain that this would win the prize. | 看起来这块饼干肯定会赢得奖品。
[01:54.310] But just before the competition closed, | 但就在比赛结束前，
[01:57.120] a lorry arrived at the factory | 一辆卡车抵达工厂，
[01:59.245] with a truly colossal biscuit which weighed 2,400 pounds. | 载着一块重达2400磅的真正巨大的饼干。
[02:05.180] It had been baked by a college student who had used over 1,000 pounds of flour, | 它是由一名大学生烘焙的，他用了1000多磅面粉，
[02:10.425] 800 pounds of sugar, | 800磅糖，
[02:12.240] 200 pounds of fat, | 200磅脂肪，
[02:14.040] and 400 pounds of various other ingredients. | 以及400磅各种其他配料。
[02:17.215] It was so heavy that a crane had to be used to remove it from the lorry. | 它太重了，不得不动用起重机才能将其从卡车上卸下。
[02:21.530] The manufacturers had to pay more money than they had anticipated, | 制造商不得不支付比他们预期更多的钱，
[02:25.850] for they bought the biscuit from the student for $4,800. | 因为他们以4800美元的价格从学生那里买下了这块饼干。
[02:31.781]